ed as soon as it has opened (and, with ",{"see":"P:Runic.Desktop.DesktopHostOptions.WaitForConnection"},", its bridge has connected). Before closing, a warning is written to standard error (and logged as event 2002 when an ",{"c":"ILoggerFactory"}," is registered) and ",{"c":"RUNIC_APPLICATION_OPENED=<presentation>"},", such as ",{"c":"Embedded"}," or ",{"c":"Chrome"},", is written to standard output. It is an automation switch for applications shaped like the ",{"c":"runic-app"}," template, which exit when their one window's ",{"see":"M:Runic.Desktop.DesktopWindow.WaitForClose(System.Threading.CancellationToken)"}," returns; other applications may keep running or reopen windows."]}},{"id":"M:Runic.Application.Views.Desktop.DesktopBridgeWindowExtensions.ValidateDesktopWindow``1(System.IServiceProvider,Runic.Desktop.DesktopHost,Runic.Desktop.DesktopWindowOptions)","kind":"method","name":"ValidateDesktopWindow","signature":["public static ",["DesktopValidationResult","T:Runic.Desktop.DesktopValidationResult"]," ValidateDesktopWindow<TViewModel>(this ",["IServiceProvider","T:System.IServiceProvider"]," services, ",["DesktopHost","T:Runic.Desktop.DesktopHost"]," desktop, ",["DesktopWindowOptions","T:Runic.Desktop.DesktopWindowOptions"],"? windowOptions = null) where TViewModel : class"],"extension":true,"docs":{"summary":["Checks at startup, before any window opens, that ",{"c":"services"}," can open a Window for ",{"c":"TViewModel"}," and that ",{"c":"desktop"}," can present it with ",{"c":"windowOptions"},"."],"remarks":["The result combines the generated Bridge registration (an error when missing) and the ViewModel registration (a warning when the container does not confirm it through ",{"see":"T:Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.IServiceProviderIsService"},"; containers without that service are not checked) with ",{"see":"M:Runic.Desktop.DesktopHost.Validate(Runic.Desktop.DesktopWindowOptions)"},". Registration failures are logged through the service provider